        "original_id": "6e728259-cbc9-51af-a822-ba9a9ccb0588",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ludwig van Beethoven, Heinrich Marschner\n- Works: Turkish March, The Elephant Never Forgets, El Chavo del Ocho\n- Topics: German classical music, German opera, cover versions, theme songs\n\nFacts:\n- Ludwig van Beethoven was baptised on 17 December 1770 and died on 26 March 1827.\n- Ludwig van Beethoven was a German composer and pianist.\n- Heinrich August Marschner was born on 16 August 1795 and died on 14 December 1861.\n- Heinrich August Marschner was considered the most important composer of German opera between Weber and Wagner.\n- The Turkish March, also titled Marcia alla turca, is a well-known classical march theme by Ludwig van Beethoven.\n- The Elephant Never Forgets is a cover version of Beethoven's Turkish March.\n- The Elephant Never Forgets was used as the theme song for El Chavo del Ocho.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
